 A reservation holds units of a SKU for a limited time while the customer pays.
 `confirm` makes the hold permanent, `release` (or expiry) returns the units.
 The service is shared by all request-handling threads in the process.
+
+Concurrency model:
+- `_guard` protects the in-process bookkeeping (`_reservations`, `_sku_locks`) and is
+  never held across a store call.
+- One lock per SKU serializes the read-modify-write on that SKU's stock, so the store
+  round trips for different SKUs still overlap.
+- A hold is claimed (popped) under `_guard` before its units are returned, so
+  `confirm`, `release` and `sweep_expired` can never act on the same hold twice.
 """
 
